{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "KJV1769",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 3,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After this opened Job his mouth, and cursed his day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Job spake, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the day perish wherein I was born, and the night ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it was said, There is a man child conceived.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let that day be darkness; let not God regard it from above, neither let the light shine upon it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let darkness and the shadow of death stain it; let a cloud dwell upon it; let the blackness of the day terrify it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that night, let darkness seize upon it; let it not be joined unto the days of the year, let it not come into the number of the months.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Lo, let that night be solitary, let no joyful voice come therein.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let them curse it that curse the day, who are ready to raise up their mourning.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let the stars of the twilight thereof be dark; let it look for light, but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "have",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none; neither let it see the dawning of the day:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because it shut not up the doors of my ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "mother’s",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " womb, nor hid sorrow from mine eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why died I not from the womb? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "why",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " did I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "not",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " give up the ghost when I came out of the belly?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why did the knees prevent me? or why the breasts that I should suck?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For now should I have lain still and been quiet, I should have slept: then had I been at rest,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With kings and counsellors of the earth, which built desolate places for themselves;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or with princes that had gold, who filled their houses with silver:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or as an hidden untimely birth I had not been; as infants ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " never saw light.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There the wicked cease ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " troubling; and there the weary be at rest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the prisoners rest together; they hear not the voice of the oppressor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The small and great are there; and the servant ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " free from his master.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore is light given to him that is in misery, and life unto the bitter ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " soul;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which long for death, but it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "cometh",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not; and dig for it more than for hid treasures;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Which rejoice exceedingly, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " are glad, when they can find the grave?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why is light given",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to a man whose way is hid, and whom God hath hedged in?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For my sighing cometh before I eat, and my roarings are poured out like the waters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the thing which I greatly feared is come upon me, and that which I was afraid of is come unto me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.3.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "KJV1769:JOB.3.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was not in safety, neither had I rest, neither was I quiet; yet trouble came.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
